course: dictionary
lesson: 5145
title: The prefix ir- means not
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some small word parts go at the start of a word and change its meaning. We call them prefixes. The prefix ir- means «not», and you use it before words that begin with r. Take the word regular, which means happening at the same pattern or times. Add ir- and you get irregular, which means not regular.
explain: Look at the pattern of the letters. «ir» is the prefix, and «regular» is the root. Ir + regular = irregular. You can see the double r: one r comes from the end of ir-, and one r starts regular. Other prefixes that mean «not» follow similar rules, so the first letter of the root tells you which one to use.
explain: Spelling clues help too. «ir», «ur» and «er» make the same sound (bird, burn, her), but each word has its own usual spelling. So when you see ir- at the start of a word, do not change its spelling just because the sound is the same. Check the root word first, then add the prefix.
fact: The prefix ir- means «not».
fact: Use ir- before words beginning with r, such as irregular (not regular), irresponsible (not responsible) and irrelevant (not relevant).
fact: The double r appears because ir + r makes two r's: ir + regular = irregular.
fact: «IR» is a short form for infrared, light just beyond red that we cannot see but feel as heat, used in TV remote controls.
fact: «Ir» is also the chemical symbol for the element iridium.
exercise: The prefix «ir-» in «irregular» means what? | again | *not | before | under
exercise: Which word is spelled with the prefix «ir-» before an r? | inactive | illegal | *irrelevant | impossible
exercise: Why does «irresponsible» have two r's? | Because it is an abbreviation | *Because ir- ends in r and responsible starts with r | Because it is a very long word | Because the word comes from Irish
test: Which prefix goes before «regular» to make a word meaning not regular? | un- | im- | *ir- | il-
test: The remote control sends «IR» signals. What does IR stand for? | International Radio | *Infrared | Internet Router | Ice Rain
exam: Which word is spelled correctly? | iressistible | iresistible | irrsistible | *irresistible
